# FLOOR 6: THE SCARLET DEVIL MANSION
## Evidence System v2 — Group Dynamics Edition

---

> **Core Philosophy:** Players don't know who is in which group at first. They learn it organically through exploration and conversation. The group structure creates both cover and contradiction — enemies hide behind their groupmates, allies are inadvertently suspicious because of who they live with. The safest-looking group (Group 1, all allies) is designed to look the most suspicious on first impression. The most tightly-knit group (Group 4, three enemies and one isolated ally) is designed to make the innocent person look like the odd one out.

---

## CAST AND GROUP STRUCTURE

| Group | Members | Alignment | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Group 1** | Ema, Hanna, Sherry | All Allies | Safest group. Designed to look suspicious at first glance. |
| **Group 2** | Alisa, Margo, Nanoka | 2 Allies / 1 Enemy | Fracture group. The allies sense something is wrong. |
| **Group 3** | Noah, An-an, Hiro | 1 Ally / 2 Enemies | Inversion group. The pair looks safe; the loner looks guilty. |
| **Group 4** | Leah, Meruru, Coco, Miria | 1 Ally / 3 Enemies | Pressure group. The one innocent person has no one vouching for her. |

