## INVESTIGATION RULES

### Talking to Groups vs. Individuals

**Group conversations** reveal surface-level alibis — the polished, rehearsed version. Enemies have coordinated. What they say in a group setting sounds consistent.

**Individual conversations** are where the cracks appear. Separate them from their groupmates and inconsistencies emerge: different timelines, hesitations, things they said that others contradict.

**DM Rule:** Never give Direct evidence during a group conversation. Circumstantial only. The Direct evidence comes from private questioning, physical exploration, or catching someone alone.

---

### The Cross-Examination — When Two NPCs Are Brought Face to Face

The party's most powerful tool. Choose two NPCs and bring them into the same conversation simultaneously.

- **Two enemies:** Their stories have been rehearsed together. They hold. But they are *too* consistent — DC 14 Insight to notice the scripted quality.
- **An enemy and an ally:** The ally contradicts the enemy without realizing it. The enemy has to improvise. This is where enemies slip. DC 12 Insight to catch the improvisation.
- **Two allies:** Freely corroborate each other. Their stories have natural variation (real memories do). No suspicious tells.

**The Tell of a Rehearsed Alibi:** Real memories have texture. Ask two people what they had for tea and they'll give slightly different answers — one says "chamomile," one says "the herbal one." Rehearsed alibis say the same thing with the same words. A DC 14 Insight check during any cross-examination detects scripted synchronization.

---

### The Trust Economy

| Action | Trust Effect |
|---|---|
| Correct accusation + valid evidence | +1 with all remaining allies |
| Wrong accusation + real evidence (misread clue) | No change |
| Accusation with no evidence | −1 with all allies present |
| Wrong accusation of an ally | −2 with that ally; −1 with all witnesses |
| Forcing open a personal item without permission | −1 with that NPC's group |
| Asking a question an ally already answered | No penalty, but they notice |

**Trust Payoff:** At Trust 2+ with any ally, they will volunteer one piece of evidence unprompted. At Trust 3+, they will name a suspect themselves if they have enough suspicion — but only if the party has already caught one enemy, proving they can handle the information.

