## CONFRONTATION SCRIPTS

*The first defense statement each enemy gives. Players must counter with evidence that directly breaks it.*

---

**NANOKA**
> *"I was in my room all evening. I didn't go near any Vessel. I don't even know where they are."*

**Broken by:** E-09 (she was seen in the east corridor near Vessel A), E-07 (she made plans for 8pm she never kept), or E-10 (she has a letter assigning her Vessel A specifically)

**Her second defense (if first isn't airtight):**
> *"Alisa was mistaken about which corridor it was. It all looks the same."*

**Counter:** The distinctive crack in the east corridor wall Alisa specifically described. The party can verify the crack is there.

---

**HIRO**
> *"An-an and I were in the sitting room all evening. Ask her yourself."*

**Broken by:** E-17 (the room was undisturbed, tea cups unused), E-15 (their timelines contradict each other)

**Her second defense:**
> *"We weren't on the sofa the whole time. We moved around. The dust doesn't prove anything."*

**Counter:** Two unused tea cups. If they were there all evening, they had tea. The cups were never filled.

---

**AN-AN**
> *"Hiro and I were together. We've already told you this."*

**Broken by:** E-16 (she knows the maze shortcut to Vessel E with no explanation), E-15 (her timeline doesn't match Hiro's)

**Her second defense:**
> *"I must have heard about the shortcut from someone. I don't remember who. That's hardly evidence."*

